WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.767
The perceptron.

2
00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:06.633
It's the simplest neural network, and its failure is why deep learning exists.

3
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.333
A perceptron is one artificial neuron.

4
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:15.267
It multiplies each input by a learned weight, adds a bias, and checks the sum.

5
00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:18.343
If the sum is positive, the output is one.

6
00:00:18.343 --> 00:00:19.400
Otherwise, zero.

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.967
Here's the computation, step by step.

8
00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.300
Inputs come in.

9
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.133
Each is scaled by its weight.

10
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:28.733
The weighted values are added with the bias.

11
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:32.900
A hard threshold decides, and the neuron outputs zero or one.

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.733
Geometrically, a perceptron draws a single straight line through input space.

13
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.407
Take the AND function.

14
00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.467
Only the point one, one is a one.

15
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.228
One straight line separates it from the rest.

16
00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:49.767
When the neuron errs, the learning rule nudges the weights toward the right answer.

17
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.090
Now the failure.

18
00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:52.933
This is XOR.

19
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:55.900
It outputs one only when the two inputs differ.

20
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.368
But the ones sit on opposite corners.

21
00:00:58.368 --> 00:01:02.000
No straight line separates them, so no weights will ever work.

22
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.000
Here's the learning rule in NumPy.

23
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.100
We predict with the weighted sum and the threshold.

24
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.523
Then we nudge the weights by the error.

25
00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:12.700
It only changes when the guess is wrong.

26
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.575
It learns AND perfectly.

27
00:01:14.575 --> 00:01:17.267
Swap in XOR, and this loop never settles.

28
00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:20.333
Here's where this bites in real work.

29
00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:26.667
A satellite telemetry alert is secretly a perceptron, a weighted sum of temperature and voltage.

30
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:31.074
Then you see readings that are normal alone but anomalous together.

31
00:01:31.074 --> 00:01:32.300
That's an XOR shape.

32
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.003
No reweighting fixes it.

33
00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:36.867
You need a hidden layer, which is our next topic.

34
00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:38.800
Let's recap.

35
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.733
A perceptron is a weighted sum with a threshold.

36
00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.567
It draws one straight line.

37
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:45.933
XOR can't be split by one line.

38
00:01:46.233 --> 00:01:48.157
The fix is to stack layers.

39
00:01:48.157 --> 00:01:50.367
Next up: neural network basics.
